    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass (the acceptance layer is the only test class in the project, and it now covers the three new address-normalization checkpoints).\n\n## Summary\n\nI introduced address normalization applied whenever an owner is created, following the codebase's established idiom (a pure normalizer utility paired with a `Normalize*` pipeline step, plus centralized comparison in `HouseholdNormalizer`).\n\n**New files**\n- `AddressNormalizer.java` \u2014 pure utility that trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands whole-word abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`); `null`/blank \u2192 `\"\"`; idempotent. Mirrors the existing `TelephoneNormalizer`/`EmailNormalizer`.\n- `NormalizeAddress.java` \u2014 pipeline step that binds the request body once, normalizes the address, and republishes the DTO. It runs **first** so the normalized value flows through the whole pipeline.\n\n**Changed files**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted `normalizeAddress` as the first step, ahead of `validate`.\n- `ValidateOwnerFields.java` \u2014 now reads the republished `@Val` DTO (no longer binds the body). Because it runs after `NormalizeAddress`, the required-field check judges the address in normalized form, so an address blank after normalization is rejected as 400.\n- `HouseholdNormalizer.java` \u2014 the address component of the household key/id now goes through `AddressNormalizer`, so duplicate detection (`EnsureUniqueHousehold`) and the shared household id (`AssignHousehold`) both compare the normalized form. The last-name comparison is unchanged (renamed the private helper to `normalizeName`).\n\n**Behavior verified by tests**\n- `\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 stored/returned as `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`.\n- `\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`.\n- `\"   \"` \u2192 rejected with 400 (blank after normalization).\n\nEach concern stays in one small unit: normalization logic lives only in `AddressNormalizer`, the step just applies it, validation stays in `ValidateOwnerFields`, and address comparison stays centralized in `HouseholdNormalizer` \u2014 no class became a catch-all. Only the create path was touched, as the spec scopes this to owner creation.",
